        "content": "#include <cassert>\n#include <cstddef>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    if (std::scanf(\"%d%d\", &n, &s) != 2) return 0;\n\n    assert(n > 0);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n\n    const std::size_t width = static_cast<std::size_t>(n);\n    std::vector<int> matrix(width * width);\n    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < matrix.size(); ++i) {\n        std::scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[i]);\n    }\n\n    // Each entry is the vertical sum for one column in the current S-row band.\n    std::vector<long long> columnSums(width, 0);\n    for (int row = 0; row < s; ++row) {\n        const std::size_t rowOffset = static_cast<std::size_t>(row) * width;\n        for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n            columnSums[col] += matrix[rowOffset + static_cast<std::size_t>(col)];\n        }\n    }\n\n    long long maxSum = 0;\n    for (int top = 0; top + s <= n; ++top) {\n        long long windowSum = 0;\n        for (int col = 0; col < s; ++col) {\n            windowSum += columnSums[col];\n        }\n        if (top == 0 || windowSum > maxSum) maxSum = windowSum;\n\n        // Horizontal windows advance with one entering and one leaving column.\n        for (int left = 1; left + s <= n; ++left) {\n            windowSum += columnSums[left + s - 1];\n            windowSum -= columnSums[left - 1];\n            if (windowSum > maxSum) maxSum = windowSum;\n        }\n\n        // Columns are independent here, allowing SIMD across the contiguous row.\n        if (top + s < n) {\n            const std::size_t leavingOffset = static_cast<std::size_t>(top) * width;\n            const std::size_t enteringOffset = static_cast<std::size_t>(top + s) * width;\n            for (int col = 0; col < n; ++col) {\n                const std::size_t index = static_cast<std::size_t>(col);\n                columnSums[index] +=\n                    static_cast<long long>(matrix[enteringOffset + index]) -\n                    matrix[leavingOffset + index];\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    std::printf(\"%lld\\n\", maxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Maintaining vertical S-row column sums reduces the scan from O(SN²) updates to O(N²) work. The flat matrix layout and independent per-column band-update loop may also improve locality and permit compiler SIMD vectorization.",
    "notes": "Uses 64-bit intermediates for rolling sums; with N < 8000 and 32-bit matrix entries, all intermediate window and column sums fit in 64 bits. No execution or timing evidence is available; evaluate correctness and speed on the controller.",
